    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "O’Farrell Property is delighted to present this impressive 4 bedroom / 3 bathroom detached home, ideally positioned on a substantial corner site with an exceptionally large private garden. Built c. 2008 and extending to c. 130m², this spacious property offers excellent accommodation both internally and externally, with the outdoor space being a particularly outstanding feature of the property.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation briefly comprises entrance hallway, spacious living room to the front, with double doors leading through to the generous kitchen / diner. This is a particularly bright and spacious room, with patio doors opening directly onto the rear garden, creating a lovely connection between the indoor and outdoor living spaces. A utility room and guest WC complete the ground floor.\r\n\r\nUpstairs there is a landing, four bedrooms, family bathroom and en-suite. The property feels bright and spacious throughout, with excellent natural light. The same flooring runs throughout the ground floor, creating a lovely sense of flow. Features include a fitted kitchen with ample storage, feature fireplace in the living room, fitted wardrobes in all bedrooms and much more.\r\n\r\nThe outdoor space is undoubtedly one of the property's most impressive features. Occupying a large corner site of approximately 0.2 acre, the property enjoys an unusually generous garden for a modern residential development.\r\n\r\nThe house is positioned on a quiet cul-de-sac with no passing traffic, providing a lovely private setting. There is extensive off-street parking to the front on a cobblelock driveway, while two separate side entrances provide excellent access to the rear and side gardens. One of these entrances is particularly wide, offering excellent potential for access to the extensive garden area.\r\n\r\nThe huge garden offers enormous flexibility and potential, with generous space for families, entertaining, children's play areas, gardening or simply enjoying the outdoors. \r\n\r\nThe size of the site also offers significant potential for future development or extension, subject to the appropriate planning permission.\r\n\r\nThe property is not overlooked to the front or rear, further enhancing the feeling of privacy and space. The front garden enjoys views overlooking the River Barrow, adding to the property's attractive setting.\r\n\r\nLocated within a mature and highly regarded development, the property enjoys the best of both worlds — a peaceful and private position with an exceptionally large garden, while still being within walking distance of local amenities and services.\r\nA rare opportunity to acquire a spacious detached family home on a substantial corner site with an exceptionally generous garden, excellent parking, private surroundings and considerable future potential.\r\n\r\nHallway\r\nTiled flooring, under stairs storage\r\n\r\nLiving Room\r\nFeature open fireplace, timber flooring, bay window, double doors to kitchen / diner\r\n\r\nKitchen / Diner\r\nModern fitted kitchen with wall & floor units, timber flooring, double doors to living room, patio doors to garden\r\n\r\nUtility\r\nTiled flooring, countertop, plumbed for appliances, back door\r\n\r\nGuest WC\r\nWC, WHB, tiled flooring\r\n\r\nLanding\r\nCarpeted\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\r\nFitted wardrobes, carpeted, to front of house, en-suite\r\n\r\nEn-suite\r\nWC, WHB, shower, tiled flooring, tiled walls\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\r\nFitted wardrobes, carpeted\r\n\r\nBedroom 3\r\nFitted wardrobes, carpeted\r\n\r\nBedroom 4\r\nTimber flooring\r\n\r\nBathroom\r\nWC, WHB, bath, shower, hot press, attic access, tiled flooring, tiled walls\r\n\r\nServices: mains water, mains sewage, electricity, gas heating\r\n\r\nEircode: R14 TK30"
      },
